{
  "name": "Runic Mastery",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "HZMOpyC4lDgZ4c0V",
  "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-carved-stone-red.webp",
  "folder": "AGPvIxqqlfyMZtXh",
  "sort": 1000000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can invoke the power of the rune inscribed on your weapon. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest. The effect depends on the rune.</p><p><strong>Blood.</strong> When a creature hits another creature you can see within 10 feet of you with an attack roll, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by your Paladin level; you then lose Hit Points equal to your Paladin level.</p><p><strong>Frost.</strong> When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one attack with an exhalation of frost in a 30-foot Cone. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 Cold damage on a failure or half as much on a success.</p><p><strong>Unholy.</strong> When you cast Summon Undead, you can modify it so that it doesn't require Concentration; its duration becomes 1 minute for that casting, the Undead Spirit has Temporary Hit Points equal to your Paladin level plus your Charisma modifier, and the first time each turn the spirit hits a creature, it deals extra Necrotic damage equal to half your Paladin level (round up).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
